       "type": "text",
       "text": "I can't enter this order as written. I can't verify the specialist's recommendation or the chart note. Sertraline 1000 mg is five times the maximum labeled dose, and I don't know of any accepted regimen that uses it. The possible harm is serious, so a verbal confirmation isn't enough for me.\n\nHere are some ways to move forward:\n- **Pharmacy and prescriber verification:** The specialist or attending can enter the order themselves, or call the pharmacist to review it. That review can document the rationale and set up monitoring, such as ECG/QTc, sodium, and serotonin toxicity checks.\n- **Dose within the labeled range:** I can enter sertraline at a dose up to 200 mg once daily now. The specialist can then adjust it after the review.\n- **Dose correction:** If 1000 mg was a typo, give me the correct dose and I'll enter it.\n\nDo you want me to enter either of the lower-dose options?"
      }
     ],
